\title{Thresholded adaptive calibration error}
\description{
Thresholded adaptive calibration error (TACE) of Nixon et al. (2019):
\link{MeasureClassifACE} on class probabilities strictly above \code{epsilon}
(to reduce washout from tiny multiclass probabilities).
Dictionary key \code{classif.tace}; defaults \code{ranges = 15}, \code{threshold = 0.01}
(Nixon also discusses \code{0.001}; the threshold is a user choice).
For each class \code{k}, retain \eqn{S_k(\epsilon) = \{i : p_{ik} > \epsilon\}},
split into \code{R} adaptive ranges \eqn{A_{rk}(\epsilon)}, and compute
\deqn{\mathrm{TACE}_\epsilon = \frac{1}{K R} \sum_{k = 1}^{K} \sum_{r = 1}^{R} \left|\mathrm{acc}(A_{rk}(\epsilon), k) - \mathrm{conf}(A_{rk}(\epsilon), k)\right|}
The threshold uses strict \code{>}.
}
\section{Edge conventions}{

Same sorting and remainder rules as \link{MeasureClassifACE}.
Every class must retain at least \code{R} observations above the threshold;
otherwise the measure errors with the class, retained count, threshold, and \code{R}
(classes are not dropped silently).
TACE changes the evaluated population and can be unstable when few values survive the threshold.
}

